<p class='header1'>Camping</p><hr>

<p class='main'><span class='emph'>Camping tips</span><br>
Camping begins 4 PM Friday July 16th.<br>
<br>
Plan ahead thoroughly. Bring more food, more water, more ice, more stuff than you think you will need. No ATM or cash machine on site. PLAN AHEAD!<br>
<br>
No ins and outs after Midnight – you must bring in all your gear and supplies by then.<br>
<br>
Camping is unlimited for this event (Tents only! No campers, RVs or trailers will be permitted)<br>
<br>
Please stay on marked trails and pathways.  Failure to do so is at your own risk.  There’s a reason why they call it wildlife (and we’re not talkin’ about the happy hardcore fanatics).<br>
<br>
Remember – it may be very warm on July 17th – Dress and pack accordingly.<br>
<br>
Feel free to bring your own mini grill, but no open fires will be allowed. <br> 
<br>
You are responsible for maintaining and leaving no garbage or damage at your camping area.  Please be courteous and clean up after yourself.<br>
<br>
Get to know your neighbors to protect yourselves from mischief and theft.<br> 
